  "tax_note": "Adult-use retail sales pay a 10.75% marijuana excise, the 6.25% state sales tax and a local option tax of up to 3%; medical marijuana is exempt from all three (Massachusetts DOR, 830 CMR 64N.1.1).",
  "summary": "Massachusetts is the largest cannabis market in New England and one of the steadiest in the country. Adult-use stores sold $139.3 million in September 2026, and adult-use sales have held at about $1.65 billion a year in both 2024 and 2025. Falling prices have been offset by steady demand, so revenue has been flat rather than shrinking. Medical sales are a smaller and declining slice, at $11.2 million in September 2026. Summer months and December are typically the busiest, while February is the slowest.",
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much cannabis does Massachusetts sell a month?",
      "a": "In September 2026, Massachusetts adult-use retailers sold $139.3 million and medical treatment centers sold $11.2 million, for $150.5 million in all, based on Cannabis Control Commission data."
    },
    {
      "q": "How much did Massachusetts sell in 2025?",
      "a": "Adult-use gross sales totaled $1.65 billion in 2025, nearly identical to $1.65 billion in 2024. Medical sales added $156.2 million."
    },
    {
      "q": "Are Massachusetts cannabis sales figures before tax?",
      "a": "Yes. The Commission reports gross sales from the Metrc tracking system, before the 10.75% excise, 6.25% sales tax and local tax are added."
    }
  ],
